---
/**
 * The redesigned footer (docs/projects/redesign/design-export/README.md §1, "Footer").
 *
 * Renders alongside the legacy Footer.astro on a redesigned route, exactly like
 * SiteHeader.astro beside Nav.astro: both are in the DOM, `.modern-skin` /
 * `.retro-skin` in retro.css show one. Retro's footer rules all hang off
 * `[data-module='footer']`, which is the other element, so nothing here can
 * reach them and nothing there can reach this. Do not set `display` on the root.
 *
 * The appearance toggle lives here as a mono link in the link row rather than as
 * the legacy pill button (Matt, 2026-08-20): the design has no appearance
 * control of its own, and the wink block sets the register for this corner of
 * the page. The MECHANICS are untouched — it is still a <button> carrying
 * `data-appearance-toggle`, and AppearanceUI.astro drives every toggle on the
 * page through one delegated listener and a querySelectorAll, so the legacy
 * button and this one stay in sync with each other and with localStorage.
 *
 * NOT SHIPPED, pending real data: the spec's fourth link, `bluesky`. There is no
 * handle to point it at, and constraint 10 says leave a placeholder rather than
 * invent one — so it is absent, not faked. One <a> and it is done.
 */
---

<footer data-module="site-footer" class="modern-skin">
  <div class="footer-inner">
    <div class="footer-bio">
      <span class="footer-name">Matt Pyle</span>
      <p class="footer-blurb">
        Growth at Temporal. Writing about accessibility, agents, and the parts of the web that are
        about to get weird.
      </p>
      <nav aria-label="Social links" class="footer-links">
        <a href="/rss.xml">rss</a>
        {/*
          The two links that leave the site say so. Same visually-hidden suffix
          the legacy footer and ArticleActions use, so the whole site announces a
          new tab the same way. No visual arrow: the design's link row is four
          plain words and an arrow on two of them reads as decoration.
        */}
        <a href="https://github.com/mattpyle" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          github<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span>
        </a>
        <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/matt-pyle" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          linkedin<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span>
        </a>
        {/* Footer only — the header nav deliberately stays at five links. */}
        <a href="/webmcp/">webmcp</a>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="appearance-toggle"
          data-appearance-toggle
          aria-label="Switch to retro mode"
        >
          Retro mode
        </button>
      </nav>
    </div>

    {/*
      The wink. Real text rather than an aria-hidden flourish: it is three short
      lines and it is the only place the footer says anything in the site's own
      voice. A div of spans, not a list — these are three lines of one joke, not
      three items.
    */}
    <div class="footer-wink">
      <span>if (agent) goto /webmcp</span>
      <span>else &#123; coffee(); read('/writing'); &#125;</span>
      <span class="wink-last">robots.txt says yes. The cat abstained.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>

<style>
  [data-module="site-footer"] {
    margin-top: 96px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    background: var(--footer-bg);
  }

  .footer-inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 40px;
    max-width: var(--shell);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 46px var(--shell-gutter) 54px;
  }

  .footer-bio {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
    max-width: 46ch;
  }

  .footer-name {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 22px;
    letter-spacing: -.02em;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .footer-blurb {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 17.5px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink-4);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .footer-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    column-gap: 20px;
    row-gap: 8px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono-plex);
    font-size: 16px;
  }

  .footer-links a,
  .appearance-toggle {
    color: var(--ink-6);
  }

  .footer-links a:hover,
  .appearance-toggle:hover {
    color: var(--agents);
  }

  /* A button that reads as a link: the control is a real <button> because it
     performs an action rather than navigating, and the design gives it the same
     weight as its neighbours. Font, size and colour are inherited from the row
     so it cannot drift from them. */
  .appearance-toggle {
    font: inherit;
    text-transform: lowercase;
    background: none;
    border: 0;
    padding: 0;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: color 240ms ease;
  }

  .footer-wink {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono-plex);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--ink-6);
    text-align: right;
  }

  .wink-last { color: var(--agents); }

  .sr-only {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    padding: 0;
    margin: -1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0);
    white-space: nowrap;
    border: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    [data-module="site-footer"] { margin-top: 56px; }

    .footer-inner {
      gap: 28px;
      padding: 34px var(--shell-gutter-mobile) 40px;
    }

    /* Left-aligned on a narrow screen: a right-aligned block under a
       left-aligned one reads as two unrelated columns once they stack. */
    .footer-wink { text-align: left; }

    /* 44px tap targets, per the mobile spec. */
    .footer-links a,
    .appearance-toggle {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      min-height: 44px;
    }
  }
</style>
